  "diagnostics": "An initial synthetic HTTP response encoded an integral float without JSON_PRESERVE_ZERO_FRACTION, so the wire fact was actually an integer; the fixture now preserves the intended float token and the unchanged strict integer guard is distinguished. An initial shell used a non-PATH daemon name and nonexistent npm script/glob, and a static launcher preceded its helper file; corrected commands are separately executed, not counted as passes. Initial focused44 and52 pre-freeze checks preceded refund-list/linked-observation additions. First full/native matrices were stopped before correcting linked Charge/PI event reporting and are not acceptance. Targeted reporting tests exposed omission of event_type from the report query projection; it now loads that field and treats linked raw refund/dispute follow-ups as review drift without misreporting minor-unit refund amounts. All final matrices use the final frozen source; pre-chain omission controls are retained as diagnostics and eight final isolated controls are rerun on the final source.",
  "scope": "Local synthetic application acceptance, not a real provider call, external charge/transfer, production migration, merchant approval or remote CI execution. Default/native profiles overlap; skips are explicit. The new native race observes both initial wallet-lock waiters AND forces both children through four GET response arrivals outside SQL before custody; assertions require one receipt/owner, one credited result, one transaction and two journal entries. It does not certify cross-wallet owner races, creator-response races, global permission/actor/all-writer closure or OS-kill/power-loss behavior. Post-custody failures are injected exceptions. A receipt proves captured funding at its observation, not merchant bank payout availability, irreversible finality, later refund/dispute absence or an atomic remote snapshot. Identity uniqueness is scoped to this lane, not every legacy callback/manual ingress. Reporting uses the latest matching Applied envelope, not arrival-order-independent event-history adjudication. Arbitrary SQL plus key compromise remains outside this application boundary. Negative/cancellation release, refunds/disputes, wider providers, production/merchant/country/legal readiness remain explicit in docs/remaining-work-part-55.md."
